course: dictionary
lesson: 4073
title: Geothermal: heat from under the ground
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Look at the words around a new word to find its meaning. «Geothermal energy uses heat from deep underground to warm water, make steam or heat homes.» The clues are heat, deep underground and warm water. Geothermal must be about heat that comes from under the ground.
explain: «Iceland, a land of volcanoes with hot rock and hot water close under the ground, gets most of its heating this way.» Volcanoes, hot rock and hot water under the ground all point the same way. Geothermal means to do with the natural heat inside the Earth.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. Swap in "heat from inside the Earth" for geothermal energy and check: «Heat from inside the Earth energy uses heat from deep underground» still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
fact: Geothermal means to do with the natural heat inside the Earth.
fact: Geothermal energy or power is electricity or heating made from underground heat, such as hot water and steam deep in the ground.
fact: «Geothermal energy» is renewable and clean, so it does not run out the way coal does.
fact: Iceland and New Zealand use a lot of geothermal energy.
fact: You can meet geothermal heat in hot springs and geysers.
exercise: «Geothermal energy uses heat from deep underground to warm water.» What does geothermal mean? | *To do with the natural heat inside the Earth | To do with light from the Sun | To do with the wind blowing across the sea | To do with cold water in rivers
exercise: «Geothermal energy uses heat from deep underground.» Where does the heat come from? | From the Sun in the sky | From the Moon | From burning wood in a stove | *Deep under the ground
exercise: Which of these is most likely to be a geothermal power station? | Wind turning big white blades on a hill | *A station that uses hot water and steam from deep in the ground | Water falling over a dam | Solar panels on a roof
test: Iceland gets most of its heating this way. What does "this way" mean? | Using wind blowing on the coast | Using sunlight through windows | *Using heat from hot rock and hot water under the ground | Burning coal in big furnaces
test: Which of these is a geothermal spring? | A sandy beach near the sea | *Hot water bubbling up from underground heat | A cold stream running down a mountain | A lake frozen in winter
exam: Geothermal heating warms a home using which source? | Heat from deep underground | Heat from cold rain | *Heat from hot water and steam deep in the ground | Heat from the Moon
